        &hellip;However, the terminology and writing styles used to describe accidents vary considerably across sectors and organisations, raising questions about the ability of automated <span class="search-hit mathjax">coding</span> systems to generalize beyond their training domain. In this paper, we evaluate the cross-sector generalization of accident-process role classification in French occupational accide&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2609.22081v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2609.22081v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
